    "updated_at": "2021-09-24T15:19:41Z",
    "body": "Bleh. I mean, in my opinion that should not make a difference, and reloading from an error page (either user or browser initiated) should just be a fresh load. That's conceptually clean and seems fine for users who would expect a fresh start IMO.\r\n\r\nBut if all browsers treat that as a special case and retain `state`/POST data/etc., then I guess we should add a special case of that sort.",
